A||||7||johnt671||Holley t.b. How easy to install on 84 duke||||5||
Z||000000||johnt671||07-25-2001||05:29 PM||||Thinking about replacing my T.B. with a Holley unit.  Anybody do this and how much of a hassle was it?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-25-2001||06:12 PM||||I had the TB off for cleaning a few months ago, i just never disconnected the throttle and TV cables. Taking off the TB itself was really easy. I never bothered with the cables though, so I wouldn't know that part.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||07-26-2001||01:34 PM||||TBI replacement can be an all day job. To just replace the TB is like a funel. The input(TB)is larger than the hole in the input header.Hence lake a funel. To get the best for your money replace the input with a Holley unit if you can find one, if not boar the existing stock input. Remember the stock TB is smaller than the Holley TB adn so is the part it fits on.Remove the input, get new gaskits and boar out the TB gasket as well as the input. Takes a long time to do the job right. Good luck and let us know haw tings turned out.( I have, onmy car a Holley TB and input as well as a Hooker header with an MSD 6A and GM Blaster coil.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000003||FieroSoul||07-26-2001||09:17 PM||||Hey fotofrank,<BR>  Can you feel a noticable difference with the Holley? I have been thinking about that mod for a while but wasn't sure if it would be worth it.||||reg||6
Z||000004||T-top Fiero||07-26-2001||10:15 PM||||I have the Holley TBI and Holley intake manifold on my 84 SE. While I don't have any hard numbers to back it up, I can definitely feel a difference for the better with the 2 added. Every little bit helps for the old 2.5.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||07-26-2001||10:50 PM||||Can you still get that intake? I know there are a few places that have the TBI, but if I can find both... YEAH baby...||||reg||1
Z||000006||T-top Fiero||07-26-2001||10:57 PM||||The intake manifold has been discontinued for a few years now. It does come up for sale occasionally on eBay. If you are lucky you may be able to find one in a junkyard or at a swap meet.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fotofrank||07-27-2001||01:28 PM||||Yes, there is a differance with the Holley TB and input. About a month or so ago I was on a trip with 5 or 6 other Fieros,V6 types, except for me and one other. The other Duke driver asked if I really had a Duke. I guess I kept up with the V6 guys pretty good and left him struggling behind. <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||12
